[
  {
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 2.98,
    "text": "In 1900, Greek sponge divers"
  },
  {
    "start": 2.98,
    "end": 5.76,
    "text": "pulled a corroded lump of bronze"
  },
  {
    "start": 5.76,
    "end": 7.92,
    "text": "from an ancient shipwreck."
  },
  {
    "start": 8.66,
    "end": 11.7,
    "text": "Hidden inside was an analog computer,"
  },
  {
    "start": 11.96,
    "end": 14.64,
    "text": "so advanced, modern science didn't"
  },
  {
    "start": 14.64,
    "end": 15.44,
    "text": "believe the Greeks"
  },
  {
    "start": 15.42,
    "end": 17.88,
    "text": "could build it until CT scans"
  },
  {
    "start": 17.88,
    "end": 20.82,
    "text": "proved it in 2006, found off"
  },
  {
    "start": 20.82,
    "end": 22.84,
    "text": "the island of Antachythera."
  },
  {
    "start": 23.32,
    "end": 25.48,
    "text": "This machine was built over 200"
  },
  {
    "start": 25.48,
    "end": 27.14,
    "text": "years ago."
  },
  {
    "start": 27.14,
    "end": 30.42,
    "text": "Inside its calcified shell were"
  },
  {
    "start": 30.42,
    "end": 32.58,
    "text": "more than 30 interlocking bronze"
  },
  {
    "start": 32.58,
    "end": 35.16,
    "text": "gears with precision triangular"
  },
  {
    "start": 35.16,
    "end": 35.96,
    "text": "teeth."
  },
  {
    "start": 36.28,
    "end": 37.98,
    "text": "A level of engineering history"
  },
  {
    "start": 37.98,
    "end": 39.78,
    "text": "textbooks claim didn't exist"
  },
  {
    "start": 39.78,
    "end": 43.26,
    "text": "until 14th century European clocks."
  },
  {
    "start": 43.82,
    "end": 46.42,
    "text": "It wasn't a timepiece. By turning"
  },
  {
    "start": 46.42,
    "end": 49.34,
    "text": "a hand crank, it calculated solar"
  },
  {
    "start": 49.34,
    "end": 51.46,
    "text": "eclipses decades in advance,"
  },
  {
    "start": 51.46,
    "end": 54.24,
    "text": "tracked the Olympic Games, and"
  },
  {
    "start": 54.24,
    "end": 56.64,
    "text": "used an epicyclic pin and slot"
  },
  {
    "start": 56.64,
    "end": 59.66,
    "text": "gear train to replicate the elliptical"
  },
  {
    "start": 59.66,
    "end": 61.3,
    "text": "speed of the moon."
  },
  {
    "start": 61.82,
    "end": 65.8,
    "text": "Over 3 ,500 ancient Greek characters"
  },
  {
    "start": 65.8,
    "end": 68.32,
    "text": "were engraved across its bronze"
  },
  {
    "start": 68.32,
    "end": 70.54,
    "text": "plates, acting as a complete"
  },
  {
    "start": 70.54,
    "end": 71.68,
    "text": "user manual."
  },
  {
    "start": 71.98,
    "end": 73.26,
    "text": "It wasn't built by aliens or"
  },
  {
    "start": 73.26,
    "end": 75.96,
    "text": "myth. It was Hellenistic genius,"
  },
  {
    "start": 76.52,
    "end": 78.66,
    "text": "which leaves one haunting question."
  },
  {
    "start": 78.66,
    "end": 81.64,
    "text": "If humanity built a mechanical"
  },
  {
    "start": 81.64,
    "end": 85.56,
    "text": "computer in 100 BC, where would"
  },
  {
    "start": 85.56,
    "end": 89.04,
    "text": "our world be today if this technology"
  },
  {
    "start": 89.04,
    "end": 91.78,
    "text": "had never been lost to the sea?"
  }
]